    "title": "Jumping X and O",
    "description": "Jumping X and O (1997), by Harry Kleinberg\n\nHere is what the program is written to do. First, a solid 6√ó6spot block appears in the upper right quadrant of the tv display. A 5√ó5 \"X\" pattern appears in the center and jumps randomly to a new location every 1/5 second. When the X overlaps the 6√ó6 block, the X disappears, an \"0\" pattern appears in the center of the screen, and repeats the process, being replaced by the X when an overlap with the block occurs. The program continues until the machine IS stopped",
    "release": "1977",
